  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% failure rate as a corrective-action trigger only, with no sales stop, no permanent market ban, and no public per-model publication, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which directly constrains Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S1 is strict (24-hour reporting for all incidents), which exposes both companies' unreported incidents."
